---
source: crates/agmem-server/tests/protocol.rs
expression: "&tools.tools"
---
[
  {
    "name": "context",
    "description": "Read this before your first move in a session: the standing instructions, who the user is, what is relevant right now, and the lessons earlier sessions paid for — as one markdown block.\n\nCall it once at the start of a session, and again when the topic shifts enough that a different set of memories matters. Pass `query` to aim the Relevant section at what you are about to do; leave it out for a general orientation. The other sections do not change with it.\n\nThe block is capped at `budget_chars` (6000 by default) and fills its sections in priority order, dropping whole entries rather than cutting one in half — so it is a briefing, not an inventory. Use `recall` for anything it left out, including the verbatim text, which never appears here.\n\nEvery line ends with its memory id. Hand that to `inspect` to see where the claim came from, or to `remember`'s `supersedes` the moment you learn it is wrong.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "budget_chars": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "How many characters the block may take, 6000 by default. Sections fill\nin priority order until it runs out; whole entries are dropped, never\ncut mid-sentence.",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "query": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "What this session is about, in words. It aims the Relevant section at\nthe work in front of you; the other three sections do not change with\nit. Leave it out for a general orientation.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "space": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "Where to look: `current` for this project, `user` for the person,\n`all` for every space, or a space name. Defaults to `current` and\n`user` together.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "type": "object"
    },
    "annotations": {
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "inspect",
    "description": "Look behind a stored memory: where it came from, what it used to say, and what the store actually holds.\n\nUse it when a recalled claim matters enough to check, when two claims disagree, or when you need to quote the original wording rather than the distilled version. `ref` takes one of: a memory id (bare, or `memory:<id>`) for the claim, its full correction history oldest-first, and the verbatim text it was distilled from; `episode:<id>` for that text with every claim drawn from it; `entity:<name>` for everything ever said about a subject, corrected claims included; `doc:<space>/<title>` for the newest document under a title, with its earlier versions listed; `docs` or `docs:<space>` to list documents and how many claims cite each; or `stats` for per-space counts. A document comes back one chunk at a time — `offset` and `limit` page through it.\n\nNothing is ever deleted here, so a claim that was corrected is still readable and still dated — which is what lets you tell a belief that changed from a belief that was always wrong.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$defs": {
        "DocKind": {
          "description": "What a document is for (schema v9, #132): a plan, a review of code or a\ndesign, a report of what was found, a probe recording an experiment, a\nverbatim transcript, or other.",
          "enum": [
            "plan",
            "review",
            "report",
            "probe",
            "transcript",
            "other"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "doc_kinds": {
          "default": [],
          "description": "For `docs`: keep only these kinds.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/DocKind"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "limit": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "For an episode: how many characters of content to return. A document\ndefaults to one chunk's worth and says in `window` where to continue;\nanonymous text comes back whole unless this is set.",
          "format": "uint",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "offset": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "For an episode: where in its content to start reading, in characters.\nDefaults to the beginning.",
          "format": "uint",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "ref": {
          "description": "What to look at: `memory:<id>` for a claim's history and the text\nbehind it, `episode:<id>` for stored verbatim text, `entity:<name>`\nfor everything said about a subject, `doc:<space>/<title>` for the\nnewest document under a title, `docs` or `docs:<space>` to list\ndocuments, or `stats` for what each space holds. Any bare id another\ncall handed you also works, whichever of those it turns out to name.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "space": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "Where to look: `current`, `user`, `all`, or a space name. Defaults to\n`current` and `user` together — or to `all` for `stats`, which is a\nquestion about the whole store.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "tags": {
          "default": [],
          "description": "For `docs`: keep only documents carrying one of these tags.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "ref"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "outputSchema": {
      "$defs": {
        "ChunkView": {
          "description": "One retrieval slice of an episode.",
          "properties": {
            "chars": {
              "description": "How many characters the slice has.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "id": {
              "description": "The record id.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "position": {
              "description": "Zero-based position within the episode.",
              "format": "uint32",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "text": {
              "description": "The slice. Absent on a document's chunks — its content is read\nthrough the window.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "id",
            "position",
            "chars"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "DecayClass": {
          "description": "How fast a memory fades between uses: `pinned` never, `slow` over\nmonths, `normal` over weeks (the default), `fast` over days and then\npruned at startup.",
          "enum": [
            "pinned",
            "slow",
            "normal",
            "fast"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "DocKind": {
          "description": "What a document is for (schema v9, #132): a plan, a review of code or a\ndesign, a report of what was found, a probe recording an experiment, a\nverbatim transcript, or other.",
          "enum": [
            "plan",
            "review",
            "report",
            "probe",
            "transcript",
            "other"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "DocumentView": {
          "description": "One document on a listing.",
          "properties": {
            "chars": {
              "description": "How many characters it has.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "cited": {
              "description": "How many live claims cite it, through `source` or `derived_from`.\nZero means nothing was learned from it, or everything learned from\nit has since been closed.",
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "created_at": {
              "description": "When it was stored, RFC3339.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "doc_kind": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/DocKind",
              "description": "What kind of document it is."
            },
            "id": {
              "description": "The record id.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "mime": {
              "description": "The content's media type, when one was recorded.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "space": {
              "description": "The space holding it.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "tags": {
              "description": "Its labels.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            "title": {
              "description": "Its name. Several documents can share one: the newest is current.",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "id",
            "space",
            "title",
            "doc_kind",
            "tags",
            "chars",
            "cited",
            "created_at"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "EpisodeView": {
          "description": "Verbatim text as stored — never rewritten, never superseded.",
          "properties": {
            "chars": {
              "description": "How many characters the whole text has.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "content": {
              "description": "The text, exactly as it was given — or the requested window of it,\nwhen `window` is present.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "created_at": {
              "description": "When the row was written, RFC3339.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "doc_kind": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/DocKind"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "What kind of document this is; absent on anonymous text."
            },
            "id": {
              "description": "The record id.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "mime": {
              "description": "The content's media type, when one was recorded.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "occurred_at": {
              "description": "When the events described happened, RFC3339.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "session": {
              "description": "The conversation or working session it belongs to.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "space": {
              "description": "The space holding it.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "tags": {
              "description": "A document's labels; absent when it has none.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": [
                "array",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "title": {
              "description": "The document's name. Present with `doc_kind`; absent on anonymous\ntext.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "id",
            "space",
            "content",
            "chars",
            "occurred_at",
            "created_at"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "Inspected": {
          "description": "One of the four answers, tagged by `kind`.",
          "oneOf": [
            {
              "description": "A claim, where it came from, and what it used to say.",
              "properties": {
                "chain": {
                  "description": "Its whole supersession chain, oldest first, this claim included. A\nclaim that has never been corrected is a chain of one; a longer one\nis a belief that changed, and each link is dated.",
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "#/$defs/MemoryView"
                  },
                  "type": "array"
                },
                "episode": {
                  "anyOf": [
                    {
                      "$ref": "#/$defs/EpisodeView"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "null"
                    }
                  ],
                  "description": "The verbatim text it was distilled from, when there is one. Quote\nfrom this rather than from the claim when precision matters."
                },
                "expands": {
                  "description": "The full records behind the claim's `derived_from` citations —\nwhat a `summary` stands in for, expanded one call deep (issue\n#85). Only memory citations expand; an episode citation stays a\nref, reachable through its own `inspect`. Absent when the claim\ncites no memories, or when every cited one has been purged.",
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "#/$defs/MemoryView"
                  },
                  "type": [
                    "array",
                    "null"
                  ]
                },
                "kind": {
                  "const": "memory",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "memory": {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/MemoryView",
                  "description": "The claim asked about."
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "kind",
                "memory",
                "chain"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "description": "Stored verbatim text and everything that came out of it.",
              "properties": {
                "chunks": {
                  "description": "The slices retrieval matches against, in reading order. On a\ndocument they carry their size and not their text: read the\ncontent through the window instead.",
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "#/$defs/ChunkView"
                  },
                  "type": "array"
                },
                "derived": {
                  "description": "The claims distilled from it or drawn from it, oldest first.",
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "#/$defs/MemoryView"
                  },
                  "type": "array"
                },
                "episode": {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/EpisodeView",
                  "description": "The text, unedited — or the window of it that was asked for."
                },
                "kind": {
                  "const": "episode",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "versions": {
                  "description": "On a document: every version stored under its title, newest\nfirst, this one included. The first is the current one.",
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "#/$defs/VersionView"
                  },
                  "type": [
                    "array",
                    "null"
                  ]
                },
                "window": {
                  "anyOf": [
                    {
                      "$ref": "#/$defs/Window"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "null"
                    }
                  ],
                  "description": "Which part of the content `episode.content` holds, when it is not\nthe whole of it."
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "kind",
                "episode",
                "chunks",
                "derived"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "description": "The documents a space holds.",
              "properties": {
                "documents": {
                  "description": "Newest first. Each carries how many live claims cite it, so an\norphan — a document nothing was learned from — is visible as such.",
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "#/$defs/DocumentView"
                  },
                  "type": "array"
                },
                "kind": {
                  "const": "documents",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "kind",
                "documents"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "description": "Everything said about one subject.",
              "properties": {
                "entity": {
                  "description": "The subject asked about.",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "kind": {
                  "const": "entity",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "memories": {
                  "description": "Every claim naming it, strongest first — closed ones included, so\na contradiction shows up as history rather than as a conflict.",
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "#/$defs/MemoryView"
                  },
                  "type": "array"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "kind",
                "entity",
                "memories"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "description": "What the store holds.",
              "properties": {
                "counts": {
                  "description": "One entry per space searched.",
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "#/$defs/SpaceCounts"
                  },
                  "type": "array"
                },
                "kind": {
                  "const": "stats",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "kind",
                "counts"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            }
          ]
        },
        "Kind": {
          "description": "What a memory is. `fact`: a distilled claim about the world, the user or\nthe project. `lesson`: a procedural insight, \"X fails when Y; do Z\".\n`instruction`: a standing rule, pinned into every briefing. `summary`: a\ndigest standing in for the claims it cites; `reflect` writes it.",
          "enum": [
            "fact",
            "lesson",
            "instruction",
            "summary"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "KindCount": {
          "description": "How many live memories of one kind a space holds.",
          "properties": {
            "count": {
              "description": "How many.",
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "kind": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Kind",
              "description": "The kind."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "kind",
            "count"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "MemoryView": {
          "description": "A memory as `inspect` renders it: the whole row, including the counters\n`recall` folds away into a score.",
          "properties": {
            "access_count": {
              "description": "How often recall has returned it.",
              "format": "uint32",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "content": {
              "description": "The claim itself.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "created_at": {
              "description": "When the row was written, RFC3339.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "decay_class": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/DecayClass",
              "description": "How fast it fades between uses."
            },
            "derived_from": {
              "description": "What this claim was reflected out of, when `reflect` wrote it: the\nmemories and episodes it was drawn from, as refs to hand straight back\nto `inspect`. Absent on a claim that cites nothing.\n\nThis is what makes a conclusion checkable rather than something to take\non faith — the evidence is named, and each piece of it has its own\nhistory to walk.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": [
                "array",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "entities": {
              "description": "The subjects it is about.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            "id": {
              "description": "The record id.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "invalid_at": {
              "description": "When it stopped; absent while it is still live.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "invalid_reason": {
              "description": "Why it stopped: `superseded`, `forgotten`, or `expired`.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "kind": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Kind",
              "description": "What the claim is."
            },
            "last_accessed": {
              "description": "When recall last returned it, RFC3339.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "source": {
              "description": "Where it came from: `agent`, `episode:<id>`, or `external:<origin>`.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "space": {
              "description": "The space holding it.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "strength": {
              "description": "Ebbinghaus stability: 1.0 when written, raised by every recall that\nreturns it. A high number on an old memory means it is still in use.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "superseded_by": {
              "description": "The claim that corrected this one.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "supersedes": {
              "description": "The claims this one corrected — several when it merged a duplicate\ncluster into one wording. Absent, not empty, when it corrected nothing\n(see the `derived_from` note above on why this is `Option`).",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": [
                "array",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "tags": {
              "description": "Its labels.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            "valid_from": {
              "description": "When the claim started being true, RFC3339.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "writer": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/WriterView"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "Who wrote the row: the MCP client, the session the write belonged to,\nand the verb that performed it. Absent on rows stored before agmem\nrecorded writers — absence means \"not recorded\", never \"unknown\nclient\" (see the `derived_from` note below on why this is `Option`)."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "id",
            "kind",
            "content",
            "space",
            "entities",
            "tags",
            "source",
            "decay_class",
            "strength",
            "access_count",
            "last_accessed",
            "valid_from",
            "created_at"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "SpaceCounts": {
          "description": "What one space holds.",
          "properties": {
            "chunks": {
              "description": "Retrieval slices of those episodes.",
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "documents": {
              "description": "Those episodes that are documents — named, typed, listed by `docs:`.",
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "episodes": {
              "description": "Verbatim episodes.",
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "invalidated": {
              "description": "Those closed — superseded, forgotten, or expired. Memories are never\ndeleted, so this is history rather than loss.",
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "live": {
              "description": "Those still live.",
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "live_by_kind": {
              "description": "Live memories per kind; a kind with none is absent.",
              "items": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/KindCount"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            "memories": {
              "description": "Every memory ever written here, live or closed.",
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "space": {
              "description": "The space these counts describe.",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "space",
            "memories",
            "live",
            "invalidated",
            "episodes",
            "chunks",
            "documents",
            "live_by_kind"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "VersionView": {
          "description": "One version of a document, in its title's chain.",
          "properties": {
            "chars": {
              "description": "How many characters it has.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "created_at": {
              "description": "When it was stored, RFC3339.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "id": {
              "description": "The record id; `inspect` it to read that version.",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "id",
            "created_at",
            "chars"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "Window": {
          "description": "Which part of an episode's content the answer holds.",
          "properties": {
            "next_offset": {
              "description": "The `offset` to send to read on from here; absent at the end.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "offset": {
              "description": "The character offset the returned content starts at.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "returned": {
              "description": "How many characters were returned.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "total": {
              "description": "How many characters the whole content has.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "offset",
            "returned",
            "total"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "WriterView": {
          "description": "Who performed the write that created a row (issue #75).",
          "properties": {
            "client": {
              "description": "The client's name from its MCP handshake; `unknown` when the session\nnever introduced itself.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "client_version": {
              "description": "The client's version, when it offered one.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "session": {
              "description": "The session the write belonged to.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "tool": {
              "description": "The verb that performed the write: `remember` or `reflect`.",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "client",
            "session",
            "tool"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        }
      },
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "found": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Inspected",
          "description": "The answer, shaped by what `ref` named."
        },
        "ref": {
          "description": "The reference this answers, in its canonical form.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "spaces": {
          "description": "The spaces that were searched.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "ref",
        "spaces",
        "found"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "annotations": {
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "recall",
    "description": "Search everything past sessions stored — distilled claims and the verbatim text behind them — before assuming, guessing, or asking something the user may already have said.\n\nCall it at the start of a session, when a new topic comes up, and before any answer that depends on what the user prefers or decided earlier. Ask in words: the wording is matched literally and the meaning semantically, so a question works better than keywords. Drop `query` to list what `entities`, `tags` or `kinds` select on their own.\n\nHits are ranked by match, by how well they have held up since last used, and by stated importance — each visible in `signals`. Every hit carries the `source` it was distilled from, which `inspect` takes as it stands. A corrected claim is absent unless you ask with `as_of` or `include_invalidated`.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$defs": {
        "Kind": {
          "description": "What a memory is. `fact`: a distilled claim about the world, the user or\nthe project. `lesson`: a procedural insight, \"X fails when Y; do Z\".\n`instruction`: a standing rule, pinned into every briefing. `summary`: a\ndigest standing in for the claims it cites; `reflect` writes it.",
          "enum": [
            "fact",
            "lesson",
            "instruction",
            "summary"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "as_of": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "What was believed at this instant, RFC3339: the claim live then, not\nwhat replaced it. Episodes recorded later stay out.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "changed_since": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "Rank claims created or corrected at or after this instant (RFC3339)\nfirst — what changed since you last looked. Soft, like `since`.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "entities": {
          "default": [],
          "description": "Keep only memories about one of these subjects.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "include_invalidated": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "Include corrected or forgotten claims. Off by default.",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "k": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "How many hits to return. Defaults to 10.",
          "format": "uint16",
          "maximum": 65535,
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "kinds": {
          "default": [],
          "description": "Keep only these kinds.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/Kind"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "query": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "What you want to know, in words — a question or a topic, not keywords.\nBoth halves of retrieval use it: the wording matches literally, the\nmeaning matches semantically. Leave it out to list what the filters\nalone select, strongest first.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "since": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "Rank claims still true at or after this instant (RFC3339) first. A\nsoft window: nothing is hidden, and `signals.temporal` reports fit.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "space": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "Where to look: `current`, `user`, `all`, or a space name. Defaults\nto `current` and `user` together.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "tags": {
          "default": [],
          "description": "Keep only memories carrying one of these labels.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "until": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "Rank claims already true at or before this instant (RFC3339) first.\nSoft, like `since`; corrected claims need `include_invalidated`.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "type": "object"
    },
    "outputSchema": {
      "$defs": {
        "Capped": {
          "description": "What the occupancy cap moved out of the page (issue #76).\n\nA page one source dominates reads exactly like a page many sources agree\non, so the cut is admitted here the way `truncated` admits `k`'s.",
          "properties": {
            "cap": {
              "description": "The most hits of this page any single source may hold.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "displaced": {
              "description": "How many over-quota hits left the page for lower-ranked ones from\nother sources.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "note": {
              "description": "The same thing in words.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "sources": {
              "description": "The sources that were over quota — the same `episode:<id>` or\n`external:<origin>` strings the hits carry, ready for `inspect`.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "cap",
            "displaced",
            "sources",
            "note"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "Cut": {
          "description": "What match quality did to the page (issue #77).\n\nThe struct-with-note shape [`Capped`] and [`Truncated`] already have: the\nnumbers are what make the note checkable.",
          "properties": {
            "best_similarity": {
              "description": "The best cosine similarity a vector arm measured on the page, absent\nwhen nothing was measured.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": [
                "number",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "considered": {
              "description": "How many hits the page held before the cut.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "kept": {
              "description": "How many hits survived; 0 is the abstention — nothing matched well\nenough to act on, which is not the same as nothing being stored.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "note": {
              "description": "The same thing in words, with the next move.",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "kept",
            "considered",
            "note"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "Dated": {
          "description": "What the temporal window did to this page (issue #78).",
          "properties": {
            "best_fit": {
              "description": "The best temporal fit on the page, absent when nothing was datable.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": [
                "number",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "changed_since": {
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "note": {
              "description": "The same thing in words.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "since": {
              "description": "The window as asked, echoed back.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "until": {
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "note"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "DocKind": {
          "description": "What a document is for (schema v9, #132): a plan, a review of code or a\ndesign, a report of what was found, a probe recording an experiment, a\nverbatim transcript, or other.",
          "enum": [
            "plan",
            "review",
            "report",
            "probe",
            "transcript",
            "other"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "DocRef": {
          "description": "The document a verbatim hit is a slice of (#134).",
          "properties": {
            "doc_kind": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/DocKind",
              "description": "What kind of document it is."
            },
            "id": {
              "description": "The document's id.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "position": {
              "description": "The hit's zero-based chunk position within it.",
              "format": "uint32",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "title": {
              "description": "Its title.",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "id",
            "title",
            "doc_kind",
            "position"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "HitKind": {
          "description": "What a hit is.",
          "oneOf": [
            {
              "const": "fact",
              "description": "A distilled statement about the world, the user, or the project.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "lesson",
              "description": "A procedural insight: \"X fails when Y; do Z\".",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "instruction",
              "description": "A standing behavioral rule.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "summary",
              "description": "A digest standing in for several claims; the refs in `covers` reach\nthem through `inspect`.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "episode",
              "description": "A slice of verbatim text, stored unedited as ground truth.",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "HitSignals": {
          "description": "The signals behind one hit's `score`, all in `[0, 1]` except `rrf`.",
          "properties": {
            "importance": {
              "description": "The standing importance of its decay class — what keeps a rarely\nmatched instruction ahead of a well matched scratch note.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "novelty": {
              "description": "How much this claim added over its nearest neighbour when it was\nwritten, in `[0, 1]` — measured once at write time, never updated.\nReported for the reader; it carries no rank weight (issue #83,\n`docs/eval/novelty-prior.md`). Absent for rows from before the store\nrecorded it, for corrections, for verbatim text, and everywhere in a\nBM25-only deployment.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": [
                "number",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "retention": {
              "description": "How much of the memory has survived its decay curve since it was last\nused. 1.0 for a pinned memory, or for verbatim text.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "rrf": {
              "description": "How well retrieval matched, fused across the text and vector arms. It\nhas no fixed scale; compare `rrf_normalized` instead.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "rrf_normalized": {
              "description": "`rrf` on a 0–1 scale against the rest of this call: 1.0 for the\nstrongest retrieval hit, 0.0 for the weakest one returned — or 0.0\neverywhere when nothing matched on words or meaning at all.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "similarity": {
              "description": "Cosine similarity between the query and this hit, when a vector arm\nmeasured it — the one signal here with an absolute scale, comparable\nacross calls. Absent for a hit only the text arms or the entity hop\nsurfaced, and everywhere in a BM25-only deployment.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": [
                "number",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "temporal": {
              "description": "How well this hit fits the `since`/`until`/`changed_since` window the\ncall carried, in `[0, 1]` — 1.0 for any overlap, decaying with the\ndistance outside it. Absent when the call had no window, or for a hit\nwith no date to judge.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": [
                "number",
                "null"
              ]
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "rrf",
            "rrf_normalized",
            "retention",
            "importance"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "RecallHit": {
          "description": "One match, with the reasoning behind its place in the order.",
          "properties": {
            "content": {
              "description": "The claim, or the verbatim slice.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "covers": {
              "description": "On a `summary` hit, the claims it stands in for — refs `inspect` takes\nas they stand, so the digest expands only when its detail is needed.\nAbsent on every other kind of hit.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": [
                "array",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "doc": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/DocRef"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "On an `episode` hit that is a slice of a document: which document,\nand where in it. `inspect` the id to read on from `position`, or\n`doc:<space>/<title>` for its newest version. Absent on slices of\nanonymous text and on every other kind of hit."
            },
            "entities": {
              "description": "The subjects this claim is about.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            "id": {
              "description": "The id of this hit. Pass it to `inspect` to see where it came from, or\nto `remember`'s `supersedes` to correct it — the latter only for a claim,\nsince an `episode` hit is a slice of verbatim text and nothing to\ncorrect.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "invalid_at": {
              "description": "When it stopped being true; absent while it is still live.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "invalid_reason": {
              "description": "Why it stopped: `superseded`, `forgotten`, or `expired`.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "kind": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/HitKind",
              "description": "What this is: a distilled claim, or `episode` for a slice of the\nverbatim text one was distilled from."
            },
            "score": {
              "description": "The final rank, combining everything in `signals`. Comparable within\none call and not across calls.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "signals": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/HitSignals",
              "description": "Why it surfaced."
            },
            "source": {
              "description": "Where it came from: `agent`, `episode:<id>`, or `external:<origin>`.\nPass it to `inspect` to read the text behind a distilled claim.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "space": {
              "description": "The space it came from.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "superseded_by": {
              "description": "The id of the claim that replaced this one.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "tags": {
              "description": "Its labels.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            "valid_from": {
              "description": "When the claim started being true, RFC3339.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "id",
            "kind",
            "content",
            "space",
            "score",
            "signals",
            "source",
            "entities",
            "tags"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "Truncated": {
          "description": "What a `k` left behind.\n\nA page of hits looks exactly like a whole store: fifty out of fifty and\nfifty out of five hundred serialise identically, so an agent that reads a\npage and reports what memory holds is right by luck. This says which of\nthe two happened, in the answer, at the moment it matters.",
          "properties": {
            "k": {
              "description": "The `k` that did the cutting.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "matching_claims": {
              "description": "How many live claims the filters select across the searched spaces,\nignoring `query` and `k`. Relevance is not counted here: this is the\nsize of the set the ranking chose from, not of what matched well.",
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "note": {
              "description": "The same thing in words, because a number is only acted on when\nsomething says why it matters.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "returned_claims": {
              "description": "How many of them this answer carries.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "matching_claims",
            "returned_claims",
            "k",
            "note"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        }
      },
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "capped": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Capped"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Present when the per-source occupancy cap changed this page: some\nsource had more strong hits than one source may hold, and the surplus\nyielded its slots to the next-ranked hits from elsewhere. Absent means\nthe page is exactly the ranking, uncapped."
        },
        "cut": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Cut"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Present when match quality changed this page (issue #77): either the\ntail fell off a marked drop in retrieval quality, or — `kept: 0` —\nnothing matched well enough to answer at all and the page is honestly\nempty. Absent means every hit earned its slot on ranking alone."
        },
        "dated": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Dated"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Present when the call carried a temporal window (issue #78): what\nwas asked, how well the page fits it, and what a soft window cannot\ndo. Absent on every call without `since`/`until`/`changed_since`."
        },
        "hits": {
          "description": "The matches, highest `score` first.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/RecallHit"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "spaces": {
          "description": "The spaces this call actually searched.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "truncated": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Truncated"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Present when this answer filled `k` and the filters select more claims\nthan it carries — so what came back is a page. Absent means `k` did not\ncut anything short: either the page never filled, or nothing beyond it\nmatches these filters."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "spaces",
        "hits"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "annotations": {
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "reflect",
    "description": "Store something you worked out from what memory already holds, together with the ids it was drawn from.\n\nCall it when reading several memories together tells you something none of them says on its own: a pattern across failures, what a preference and a constraint mean taken together, the reason behind a decision. This is the verb for a conclusion you reached; `remember` is for something you were told, and an insight with nothing behind it is a `remember` call. The cited ids are shown by `inspect`, so a later session can check the evidence still stands.\n\nStored as a `lesson` unless you say otherwise. `kind: \"summary\"` is a digest of the cited claims: `context` shows it in their place under budget pressure and `inspect` expands them, so compressing a finished session this way costs no detail.\n\nReturns the id. `created: false` means an equivalent insight was already there — read its `content`, and if yours differs, send it again with `supersedes` set to that id. `related` carries nearby live claims with their text, for the same decision.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$defs": {
        "Kind": {
          "description": "What a memory is. `fact`: a distilled claim about the world, the user or\nthe project. `lesson`: a procedural insight, \"X fails when Y; do Z\".\n`instruction`: a standing rule, pinned into every briefing. `summary`: a\ndigest standing in for the claims it cites; `reflect` writes it.",
          "enum": [
            "fact",
            "lesson",
            "instruction",
            "summary"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "derived_from": {
          "description": "The ids it was drawn from — memory or episode ids, as `recall`,\n`remember`, `context` or `inspect` handed them to you. At least one.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "entities": {
          "default": [],
          "description": "Subjects it is about (\"user\", \"project-x\"), for filtered recall.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "insight": {
          "description": "The insight: one atomic, self-contained statement in the third\nperson. What you concluded, not the reasoning.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "kind": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Kind"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "description": "Defaults to `lesson`. `summary` is a digest standing in for the cited\nclaims: `context` shows it in their place under budget pressure."
        },
        "space": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "Where to store: this server's space by default, or `user` for what\nfollows the person across every project.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "supersedes": {
          "default": [],
          "description": "Ids of live claims this replaces: each is closed, stays readable and\ndated, and a list merges them.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "tags": {
          "default": [],
          "description": "Free labels. `identity` marks a fact for every session's profile.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "insight",
        "derived_from"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "outputSchema": {
      "$defs": {
        "AlreadyClosed": {
          "description": "A `supersedes` target whose close predates this call.",
          "properties": {
            "id": {
              "description": "The id that was sent in `supersedes`.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "reason": {
              "description": "Why it was already closed: `superseded`, `forgotten` or `expired`.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "superseded_by": {
              "description": "The memory that replaced it, when the reason is a supersession — the\nlive claim is there (or further down its chain), not here.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "id"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "Related": {
          "description": "A live claim near the insight that was just stored.",
          "properties": {
            "content": {
              "description": "What it says, so the two can be judged without a second lookup.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "id": {
              "description": "The id of the older claim — what to put in `supersedes`.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "similarity": {
              "description": "Cosine similarity between the two, below the duplicate threshold and\nabove the floor for being worth mentioning at all.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "id",
            "content",
            "similarity"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        }
      },
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "already_closed": {
          "description": "`supersedes` targets that were already closed when this call arrived —\nskipped and reported, never rewritten, exactly as `remember` does.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/AlreadyClosed"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "content": {
          "description": "What is stored under `id` — your wording when it was written, the\nexisting claim's when it was not.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "created": {
          "description": "Whether the row was written now.\n\n`false` means an equivalent insight was already stored and nothing\nchanged. Read `content`: if it says something other than what you sent,\nyours is a correction rather than a repetition, and it is still unsaid\nuntil you send it again with `id` in `supersedes`.",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "derived_from": {
          "description": "The evidence recorded with the insight, as refs `inspect` takes as they\nstand.\n\nEmpty when `created` is false: nothing was written, and the claim\nalready under `id` keeps whatever evidence it was written with.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "id": {
          "description": "The insight's id — newly minted, or the id of the claim that already\nsaid this.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "note": {
          "description": "What to do about a write that did not happen, when there is something\nworth doing.\n\nIt appears when the insight was judged a duplicate of a claim that\n**carries no evidence of its own** — the conclusion is already stored,\nits provenance is not, and nothing here rewrites a stored claim. A\nno-op that leaves an uncited conclusion standing is not the same\noutcome as one that leaves a cited one standing, and only this says so.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "related": {
          "description": "Live claims near the insight, which it may be correcting.\n\nThese were **not** blocked and are not duplicates — they are here\nbecause a correction and the claim it corrects are near neighbours, and\nthis is the only moment the older one's id is in front of you. If one\nof them is what your insight replaces, send the insight again with its\nid in `supersedes` — several ids if several of them are the same claim\nworded differently. If it is merely related, ignore it.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/Related"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "superseded": {
          "description": "The ids of the claims closed by a `supersedes` in this call.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "created",
        "content",
        "derived_from",
        "related",
        "superseded",
        "already_closed"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "idempotentHint": true
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "remember",
    "description": "Store what this session learned — distilled claims, optionally with the verbatim text they came from — so the next session starts with it instead of working it out again.\n\nCall it as soon as something durable is said, unprompted: a preference or a standing instruction, a decision and the reason behind it, a convention, a constraint, a lesson from a failure. Nothing you say persists — an answer that ends \"noted\" without this call is a promise the next session cannot keep.\n\nDistil before you call: one atomic, self-contained claim per entry, in the third person, understandable with no conversation around it. Do not store what the code or the ticket already records, or what only matters to this turn.\n\nNothing here is rewritten. When a stored claim turns out to be wrong, send the correction with `supersedes` set to its id rather than storing a contradiction: the old claim stays readable and dated, and only one is live.\n\nReturns a diff, not an acknowledgement: `created`, `duplicates` (**not** written) and `related`, the last two with the id and text of a claim already stored. Read both before you answer: a correction reads much like the claim it corrects, so it lands there rather than in `created`, and reporting it as remembered would leave the old, wrong claim live. When one of them contradicts yours, send yours again with `supersedes` set to its id.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$defs": {
        "DecayClass": {
          "description": "How fast a memory fades between uses: `pinned` never, `slow` over\nmonths, `normal` over weeks (the default), `fast` over days and then\npruned at startup.",
          "enum": [
            "pinned",
            "slow",
            "normal",
            "fast"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "DocKind": {
          "description": "What a document is for (schema v9, #132): a plan, a review of code or a\ndesign, a report of what was found, a probe recording an experiment, a\nverbatim transcript, or other.",
          "enum": [
            "plan",
            "review",
            "report",
            "probe",
            "transcript",
            "other"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "EpisodeInput": {
          "description": "Verbatim ground truth to store alongside what was distilled from it.",
          "properties": {
            "content": {
              "description": "The text, unedited. It is chunked for retrieval but never rewritten.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "doc_kind": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/DocKind"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "default": null,
              "description": "What kind of document. Needs `title`; no `transcript` in `user`."
            },
            "mime": {
              "default": null,
              "description": "Media type, such as `text/markdown`.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "occurred_at": {
              "default": null,
              "description": "When it happened, RFC3339. Defaults to now.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "session": {
              "default": null,
              "description": "A grouping key for one session.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "tags": {
              "default": [],
              "description": "Labels a document is listed by.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            "title": {
              "default": null,
              "description": "Names the episode as a document claims can cite; a later one under\nthe same title is a newer version. Needs `doc_kind`.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "content"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "Kind": {
          "description": "What a memory is. `fact`: a distilled claim about the world, the user or\nthe project. `lesson`: a procedural insight, \"X fails when Y; do Z\".\n`instruction`: a standing rule, pinned into every briefing. `summary`: a\ndigest standing in for the claims it cites; `reflect` writes it.",
          "enum": [
            "fact",
            "lesson",
            "instruction",
            "summary"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "MemoryInput": {
          "description": "One claim to store.",
          "properties": {
            "content": {
              "description": "One atomic, self-contained statement in the third person — it has to\nstill make sense with no conversation around it. \"The user prefers Rust\nover Python for CLI tools\", not \"he said he likes it better\".",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "decay_class": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/DecayClass"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "default": null,
              "description": "How fast it fades. Defaults by kind: facts `normal`, lessons `slow`,\ninstructions `pinned`."
            },
            "entities": {
              "default": [],
              "description": "Subjects it is about (\"user\", \"project-x\"), for filtered recall.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            "kind": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/Kind"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "default": null,
              "description": "What the claim is; defaults to `fact`. `summary` is `reflect`'s."
            },
            "supersedes": {
              "default": [],
              "description": "Ids of live claims this replaces: each is closed, stays readable and\ndated, and a list merges them. Prefer this to `forget` for anything\nthat was once true.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            "tags": {
              "default": [],
              "description": "Free labels. `identity` marks a fact for every session's profile.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            "valid_from": {
              "default": null,
              "description": "When it became true, RFC3339. Defaults to now.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "content"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        }
      },
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "episode": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/EpisodeInput"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "The verbatim text these came from, stored unedited; every memory in\nthe call is provenanced to it."
        },
        "memories": {
          "description": "The distilled claims, one per entry. Empty only with an `episode`.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/MemoryInput"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "space": {
          "default": null,
          "description": "Where to store: this server's space by default, or `user` for what\nfollows the person across every project.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "memories"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "outputSchema": {
      "$defs": {
        "AlreadyClosed": {
          "description": "A `supersedes` target whose close predates this call.",
          "properties": {
            "id": {
              "description": "The id that was sent in `supersedes`.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "reason": {
              "description": "Why it was already closed: `superseded`, `forgotten` or `expired`.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "superseded_by": {
              "description": "The memory that replaced it, when the reason is a supersession — the\nlive claim is there (or further down its chain), not here.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "id"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "Duplicate": {
          "description": "A claim that was already in the store.",
          "properties": {
            "content": {
              "description": "What the stored memory actually says.\n\nCompare it against what you sent: if it says something different, this\nis a claim you are correcting rather than one you are repeating, and it\nis still live until you re-send yours with `id` in `supersedes`.\nIn BM25-only mode this is your own text, which matched exactly once\ncase and whitespace were folded.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "id": {
              "description": "The id of the memory that already holds this claim.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "of": {
              "description": "Which entry of the `memories` you sent this refers to, zero-based.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "similarity": {
              "description": "How close the two are, as cosine similarity.\n\nText identical to what is stored reads a rounding error *short* of 1.0\n— 0.9999998 is typical — because verbatim input trips the vector gate\nas its own nearest neighbour before the content hash is ever consulted.\nExactly 1.0 means the hash matched with no embedding to compare it\nagainst, which is BM25-only mode.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "id",
            "of",
            "content",
            "similarity"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "Related": {
          "description": "A live claim near one that was just stored.",
          "properties": {
            "content": {
              "description": "What the older memory says, so the contradiction can be judged without\na second lookup.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "id": {
              "description": "The id of the older memory — what to put in `supersedes`.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "of": {
              "description": "Which entry of the `memories` you sent this is a neighbour of,\nzero-based.",
              "format": "uint",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "similarity": {
              "description": "Cosine similarity between the two, below the duplicate threshold and\nabove the floor for being worth mentioning at all.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "id",
            "of",
            "content",
            "similarity"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        }
      },
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "already_closed": {
          "description": "`supersedes` targets that were already closed when this call arrived.\n\nNothing was rewritten for these — a supersede never rewrites another\nclose, so each keeps its original date, reason and successor, named\nhere. Usually this means the correction already happened (a retried\ncall, or another session got there first); check `superseded_by`\nbefore assuming anything is still open.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/AlreadyClosed"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "created": {
          "description": "Ids of the memories stored, in the order they were sent, skipping the\npositions reported in `duplicates`.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "duplicates": {
          "description": "The claims judged already stored. Nothing was written for these.\n\n**Read `content` before treating one as a no-op.** A correction is\nusually worded much like the claim it corrects, so it lands here too —\nand then nothing has changed, the older and now-wrong claim is what is\nstill live, and saying \"already noted\" would be false. If `content`\nsays something other than what you sent, re-send yours with the id\nhere in `supersedes`.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/Duplicate"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "episode": {
          "description": "Id of the episode, whether it was written now or already stored.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "related": {
          "description": "Live claims about the same subject as something you just stored, which\nthe new claim may contradict.\n\nThese were **written** — they are not duplicates and nothing was\nblocked. They are here because a correction and the claim it corrects\nare near neighbours, and this is the only moment the id of the older\none is in front of you. If one of these is now wrong, re-send the new\nclaim with its id in `supersedes`: that closes the old one instead of\nleaving both live and contradicting each other. If several of them are\nthe same claim in different words, send every id — one call closes them\nall. If it is merely related, ignore it.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/Related"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "superseded": {
          "description": "Ids of the memories closed by a `supersedes` in this call.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "created",
        "duplicates",
        "related",
        "superseded",
        "already_closed"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "idempotentHint": true
    }
  }
]
